From 02d4ece2fc5b0a675b8629bad4333bdb171901b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:50:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GBA link: remove all in-game back-out advice

The stuck-entry hint misfired twice on device: during the live socket-3
handoff (press-silent by design -- it advised aborting 2.5 s before
success) and on the boot menu (any long menu idle trips a press-silence
timer). Root problem: the wire looks identical whether the player is
parked at the connect screen or idling on any other menu -- XD polls the
sockets constantly either way -- so no heuristic here can place the
advice correctly. Remove the OSD hint and the bottom-screen footer
variant entirely; the recovery rule (a link arms within seconds of a
good entry; ~20 s of nothing means back out with B and re-enter) lives
in the launcher tip and the release notes, where it cannot interrupt a
working session. The roll-state log lines still record every park.
---
 .../features/dualscreen/GbaScreenView.kt      | 27 ++++---------
 .../xdnetplay/ui/XDLauncherActivity.kt        |  6 ++-
 Source/Core/Core/HW/GBADetectLog.cpp          |  6 ---
 Source/Core/Core/HW/GBADetectLog.h            |  7 +---
 Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp    | 38 +++++++------------
 5 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)

